1
00:00:02,290 --> 00:00:05,510
Our neighbor was trying to get the cats in her backyard fixed,

2
00:00:05,510 --> 00:00:11,150
but she couldn't find a low-cost spay-neuter appointment, so those cats had more cats.

3
00:00:12,190 --> 00:00:16,690
Cats in the street or in overcrowded shelters are symptoms of an equity problem.

4
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:24,080
50% of pet-owning households in the U.S. can no longer afford a basic vet visit.

5
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:30,260
And this lack of affordable services disproportionately impacts families right here in New York,

6
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:33,720
particularly low-income pet owners and communities of color.

7
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:38,320
That's why we're building a brand new non-profit veterinary clinic in Brooklyn,

8
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:41,200
and we need your help to get the doors open.

9
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:45,460
This isn't just an idea. We're finishing construction right now.

10
00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:50,660
We need your support to complete the build-out, purchase remaining medical equipment,

11
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:53,080
hire the rest of our veterinary team,

12
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:59,820
and make these critical services available and affordable to thousands of New Yorkers for years to come.

13
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:04,220
Your generosity will help give more cats the life they all deserve

14
00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:10,120
and more families the chance to enjoy the love and companionship that our pets provide.

15
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:17,360
We're so close to opening our doors, but only you can help us take the final steps.

16
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:20,660
Please donate today.

